# Memory editor

## Tabs

- Editor tabs are **always horizontal** (main tabs and Loop sub-tabs).
- Never use a vertical tab rail for memory pages.
- Tab set may change; keep Info / Loop first. Start new work on **Loop**.

## Controls

Match `ParamDef.kind` (do not invent a second widget):

| Kind | Widget |
| --- | --- |
| `enum` | `<select>` |
| `int` | range slider + numeric readout |
| `bool` | switch (ON/OFF), not a select or slider |

On/off values inside an enum of only OFF/ON also use a switch.

Layout: labels sit **above** the control. Parameters flow in a responsive column grid (`.param-columns`). Switches have no outer box — only the track.

## Icons and help

- Use the bundled MDI set (`web/src/components/Icon.tsx` + `iconify-mdi.json`), same pattern as gm-800-editor.
- To add an icon: copy the glyph from `@iconify-json/mdi` into `iconify-mdi.json` and add a name in `ICONS`.
- Every parameter with Parameter Guide text gets an **Info** icon (`InfoTip`). Click toggles the explanation; hover tooltips are optional extras.

## Sources

- Parameter names, ranges, and InfoTip text: public Boss RC-600 Parameter Guide.
